  "body": "Part of #372; needs the machine-file axis direction (#373).\n\nWhen a machine axis is inverted, the controller's coordinate system is the mirror of the CAM frame in that axis. The post must translate, not just negate:\n- write the inverted axis's coordinates and its arc-centre offset (I/J/K) with the opposite sign;\n- an arc in a plane that contains exactly one inverted axis reverses its sense in controller coordinates: **G2 <-> G3** (two inverted axes in the plane cancel);\n- cutter compensation side swaps the same way: **G41 <-> G42**;\n- work-offset values and any probe / tool-length data that carry that axis follow the same sign rule.\n\nRefuse by name (until verified per dialect): helical/thread cycles, polar/G12.1, rotary or 4/5-axis motion involving the inverted axis, and any canned cycle whose direction depends on axis sense.\n\n**Done means:** implemented in the post engine (one place, not per script) or per shipped `.cps` with a shared helper; conformance goldens for an inverted-X Fanuc and Haas program covering lines, G2/G3 in G17/G18/G19, I/J/K, G41/G42; a test that a physically identical path is produced (simulate the controller's interpretation of the posted program and compare with the CAM path); refusals pinned.",
